      "why": "iterative is the canonical low-area CORDIC (shared datapath, no per-stage registers). It is the prime candidate for the min-luts_plus_ffs selection rule. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) is the binding constraint: with W=12 the output LSB is 2^-10, so truncation alone can violate the bound and rounding is needed; with W=13 the LSB is 2^-11 giving margin. I keep n_iter at 12-14 (enough micro-rotations to converge to the LSB) and angle_guard/frac_guard at the low end to avoid overspending area on guard bits, per the advisory to sit at the accuracy floor. This is the most likely home of the selected design, so it gets the largest share."
